  "operative_text": "Section 1 (N.D.C.C. new section to chapter 62.1-01, subsection 2): A personal firearm, firearm accessory, or ammunition manufactured commercially or privately in the state and which remains within the state is not subject to federal law or federal regulation, including registration.\nSection 1 (N.D.C.C. new section to chapter 62.1-01, subsection 4): Firearm accessories imported into the state from another state, which are subject to federal regulation as being in interstate commerce, do not subject a firearm to federal regulation.\nSection 1 (N.D.C.C. new section to chapter 62.1-01, subsection 6): A firearm manufactured or sold in the state under this section must have the words \"Made in North Dakota\" clearly stamped on the receiver or frame."
}